{
  "what": "The parent/subtask status coupling of shared/taskCascade.ts, as a table: the status a parent derives from its children, the writes a status change plans (root, then descendants, then ancestors, IN ORDER), the writes a re-derivation after a subtask was created or deleted plans, and the \"started → pin to today\" companion date. Measured from the TypeScript before the port.",
  "why": "A check-off on the phone and the same check-off on the desktop must plan the same writes in the same order, and a frontend that is not JavaScript has to plan them too. The core answers WRITES (ids and states, never wording) and reads no clock: today travels in as `todayKey`.",
  "writtenBy": [
    "src/state/taskCascade.measure.test.ts — a one-off, run once and deleted; its cases mirror src/state/taskCascade.test.ts plus the rows the port needs that those never had (the exact write order, the unchanged-level stop of the cascade versus the climb-through of the recompute, an absent root, an orphan parent, the empty parent id, the empty today key, the empty scheduled date, every presence set of the four states)."
  ],
  "readBy": [
    "src/state/taskCascade.contract.test.ts",
    "crates/cal-core/src/task_cascade.rs (once the port exists)"
  ],
  "whereItLives": {
    "note": "Inside cal-core, like taskStatus.json: twelve adapter repositories compile cal-core, and an include_str! reaching out of the crate would break the day it moves."
  },
  "notInThisTable": {
    "todayIsoKey": "the clock stays on the surface; the core takes `todayKey` as a parameter (tests/core_contracts.rs)",
    "canStoreInProgress_effectiveForList": "whether a provider can hold in_progress and which per-list setting applies decide WHETHER the caller passes a today key and the coupling flag — the surface’s",
    "filter(w => w.taskId !== taskId)": "the editor and the mobile toggle drop the root write because they write the root themselves — the caller’s, not the planner’s",
    "applyStatusWrites_applyCascade": "persisting the writes and announcing the outcome (DESIGN §9.1, \"alles versuchen, dann berichten\") — the surface’s",
    "collectDescendants": "a different function in TaskDialog and taskToggle, not this module"
  },
  "shape": {
    "autoDate": "{newStatus, currentScheduledDate, todayKey} → the day to pin or null. `null` in the input means omitted.",
    "derive": "{children: [status…]} → the derived parent status or null (no children). One child per entry.",
    "cascade": "{tasks, taskId, newStatus, options?} → [{taskId, status, scheduledDate?}…] in application order: the root, its descendants, its ancestors nearest first.",
    "recompute": "{tasks, parentId, options?} → the same writes for a re-derivation starting at parentId, climbing to the root.",
    "options": "{cascadeEnabled?: boolean (absent = true), todayKey?: \"YYYY-MM-DD\" (absent = the auto-date setting is off)}",
    "baseTask": "the Task every case’s `tasks` entries are overrides over"
  },
